tion": [1304, 1206]}, "title": "\ud83c\uddfa\ud83c\uddf8 I Thank God every day knowing his divine actions saved President Trump \ud83c\uddfa\ud83c\uddf8", "last_comment_created": 1789223049919, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 2, "score_up": 34, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0GEOTUS \u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATVHReB1t", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 26, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8831491, "raw_content": "Thank you President Trump!  Where did all the students go? \r\n\r\nThe streets are safer from criminals (killers, literally) and the streets are safe 'cause most of the 3rd world scooter traffic is gone. \r\n\r\nMeanwhile,\r\n\r\n\"Miami-Dade district Superintendent Rafael Villalobos put a temporary pause on a process that could have shut down operations at 27 schools.\r\n\r\nThe school board voted to close nine schools last year, and 27 were recently being evaluated to determine whether they should \"remain operational,\" according to the Attendance Boundary Committee. The committee released a list of schools broken into two categories \u2014 those that are \"reassessed,\" and those that are \"under review.\"\r\n\r\n\"I'd like to be given that opportunity to put a pause, and then we can come back second week of October and still finish by December,\" Villalobos said at a Sept. 2 School Board Committee Meeting.\"\r\n\r\nhttps://www.usatoday.com/story/news/state/florida/miami/2026/09/03/miami-dade-superintendent-schools-closing-paused/91590313007/s", "author": "phibetared", "created": 1789227449720, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Mungo", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Where did they go? Miami Votes to Consider Closing 27 Schools!", "last_comment_created": 1789230137161, "content": "<p>Thank you President Trump!  Where did all the students go?</p>\n<p>The streets are safer from criminals (killers, literally) and the streets are safe 'cause most of the 3rd world scooter traffic is gone.</p>\n<p>Meanwhile,</p>\n<p>&quot;Miami-Dade district Superintendent Rafael Villalobos put a temporary pause on a process that could have shut down operations at 27 schools.</p>\n<p>The school board voted to close nine schools last year, and 27 were recently being evaluated to determine whether they should &quot;remain operational,&quot; according to the Attendance Boundary Committee. The committee released a list of schools broken into two categories \u2014 those that are &quot;reassessed,&quot; and those that are &quot;under review.&quot;</p>\n<p>&quot;I'd like to be given that opportunity to put a pause, and then we can come back second week of October and still finish by December,&quot; Villalobos said at a Sept. 2 School Board Committee Meeting.&quot;</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/state/florida/miami/2026/09/03/miami-dade-superintendent-schools-closing-paused/91590313007/s\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/state/florida/miami/2026/09/03/miami-dade-superintendent-schools-closing-paused/91590313007/s</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 5, "score_up": 26, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards